<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39528" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικάθ-ημαι</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικαθ-κάτημαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sit</i>
			<i>upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.72
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1093
			</span></i>; <i>press upon, be heavy upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					1046
				</span></i>
			: also c.acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καμήλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Syr.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις . . λόφον ἐπικαθημένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.14
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>sit upon</i> eggs, <i>incubate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				558a19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				619b14
			</span></i>; of bees, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐπὶ τοῖς
			κηρίοις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				625a5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐπὶ τῆς τραπέζης</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τῇ τρ</span>
			.) <i>sit at</i> his counter, of a banker's clerk or
			money-changer, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				49.17
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				33
			</span></i>: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐπικαθήμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					36.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>. of rain,
				<i>cling</i> to a flower, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.24.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. <i>sit
				down against</i> a place, <i>besiege</i> it, abs., <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.27
			</span></i>: c.dat., <i><span class="en">
				App.
			</span></i><i>Mith..</i><i><span class="en">
				78
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικαθήμενοι</span>, οἱ, <i>settlers, residents,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PTeb.
				391.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
